WEBVTT

00:00:01.111 --> 00:00:04.667
You planned to be home before dark,
but something small went wrong.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.000
A twisted ankle, a wrong turn,
or a storm that arrived early.

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:12.556
Now the night is coming,
and you are still out.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.700
Stop while you still have energy.

00:00:15.922 --> 00:00:19.700
Find shelter from the wind,
behind a boulder or a snowdrift.

00:00:20.844 --> 00:00:25.733
Three things steal your warmth:
wind, the cold ground, and wet clothes.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.733
So deal with all three.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.544
Pull a wind sack over you.

00:00:30.878 --> 00:00:34.211
It weighs about half a kilo,
and it stops the wind.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:39.466
Sit on your sleeping pad or your pack,
never straight on the snow.

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.833
Put dry layers on top,
and a dry hat on your head.

00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:45.833
Eat, and drink something warm.

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:48.755
If you need help, call early.

00:00:49.311 --> 00:00:52.755
In Norway, the emergency number is 112.

00:00:54.011 --> 00:00:58.566
A wind sack, a sleeping pad, a sleeping bag,
and in winter, a shovel.

00:00:59.344 --> 00:01:02.900
Four things in the pack, that turn
a dangerous night into a long one.

